\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere some coefficients are nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]=1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffa659c2b26ee2ff8d90b4ec9ad1725f2f5004d9a5453442ed49fc05e6352b90"} {"question" "q-107536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$\n- ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$\n- ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{1}+{c}_{3}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains a vector from another vector space.\n\n- Statement II is false. The set ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{2}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}({c}_{1}+{c}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}){c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{1}+{c}_{3}}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $C$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{1}+{c}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}{c}_{3}=({x}_{1}-{x}_{3}){c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}+{x}_{3}({c}_{1}+{c}_{3})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffa659c2b26ee2ff8d90b4ec9ad1725f2f5004d9a5453442ed49fc05e6352b90"} {"question" "q-107587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071832/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3277c6df2a340945929dc731c59ba06fafdee69f2babf7cc02d643e1a70b7e6"} {"question" "q-107587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/lin